description:
Answer a free-text question about a real-world location in one call. Signed satellite, elevation, water and built-up receipts support the answer. The tool sends the place and the question through the locate, recall and algorithm chain on the server, and returns one packaged envelope.

When to use: Call this when the question is about a specific place and the answer must carry its evidence. Send the question as `q`, with `place`, `cell` or `lat`+`lng`. Over MCP a point answer is a projection. It has `answer`, `receipt` (cite `receipt.fact_cids`), `place_resolved`, `routed_to`, `facts_summary`, `algorithm_outcomes_summary`, `spatial_trace` and `scene_url`. It has `model_answer` if you sent `model`, and `_projection`, which names what the projection removed. POST /v1/ask has more: `caveats`, `topic_routing`, `reasoning`, and `inventory` with include:["inventory"]. A `routed_to` other than answer comes back complete. The answer gives a current value. For how X changed, use emem_intent did_change or emem_diff.

Example arguments: {"q":"is this neighbourhood flood-prone for a flat purchase","place":"Ashok Nagar, Ranchi"}
